              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dastmâl is dast, \"hand\", with -mâl, \"rubbing\" (from mâlidan, \"to rub\"): the hand-wiper. Both are native Persian. (EtymDB links it to Arabic māl, \"property\", a different word that looks alike.)"
